  "answer_text": "Here is an overview of **wakehealth.edu** \u2014 the website for **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist**:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfe5 Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist\n\nAtrium Health Wake Forest Baptist is a nationally recognized, fully integrated academic medical center and health system located in **Winston-Salem, North Carolina**.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd11 Key Components\n\nThe organization's two main components are:\n1. An **integrated clinical system** anchored by Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist Medical Center, an **885-bed tertiary-care hospital** in Winston-Salem, which includes **Brenner Children's Hospital**, five community hospitals, more than 300 primary and specialty care locations, and more than 2,700 physicians.\n2. **Wake Forest University School of Medicine**, a recognized leader in experiential medical education and groundbreaking research.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf10 Part of a Larger Network\n\nAtrium Health Wake Forest Baptist is part of **Advocate Health**, the **third-largest nonprofit health system** in the United States. Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist employs more than **20,000 teammates**, part of Advocate Health's 150,000 teammates.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd2c Specialties & Services\n\nSpecialties include **Preventive Care, Specialized Care, Children's Hospital, Comprehensive Cancer Center, Digestive Health Center, Heart Center, Neurosciences, Orthopaedics, Transplantation, Level I Trauma Center, and Urology**.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udc9b Community Impact\n\nAtrium Health Wake Forest Baptist provided a record-setting **$611.2 million in community benefits** during the 2021 fiscal year, which includes unreimbursed care, charity care, education and research, and community health improvement.\n\n---\n\nYou can visit their official website at **[wakehealth.edu](https://www.wakehealth.edu)** for more information on patient care, research, education, and careers. Is there something specific about Wake Forest Baptist you'd like to know more about?",
